      "text": [
        " : سَأَلْتُ أَبَا اَلْحَسَنِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَنْ قَوْلِ اَللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ\n«۝ وَ مَنْ كٰانَ فِي هٰذِهِ أَعْمىٰ فَهُوَ فِي اَلْآخِرَةِ أَعْمىٰ وَ أَضَلُّ سَبِيلاً ۝» فَقَالَ «نَزَلَتْ فِيمَنْ سَوَّفَ اَلْحَجَّ حَجَّةَ اَلْإِسْلاَمِ وَ عِنْدَهُ مَا يَحُجُّ بِهِ فَقَالَ اَلْعَامَ أَحُجُّ اَلْعَامَ أَحُجُّ حَتَّى يَمُوتَ قَبْلَ أَنْ يَحُجَّ»."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2933 - Muhammad ibn al-Fudhayl narrated:\nI asked Abu al-Hasan (as) about the words of Allah (swt), the Exalted: \"And whoever is blind in this [life] will be blind in the Hereafter and more astray in way\" (Surah Al-Isra 17:72).\nImam (as) said: \"This verse was revealed concerning those who procrastinate the Hajj of Islam while possessing the means to perform it. They say, 'I will go next year, I will go next year,' until they die without performing Hajj.\""
        ]
      }
